  "term": "retinol",
  "definition": "Retinol is a fat-soluble form of vitamin A. It is important for normal retinal function, growth and tissue differentiation, reproductive organ function, and immune system regulation, and it acts through retinoid receptors to influence cell differentiation and programmed cell death in some cancer cells.",
